setup:
step 1: create a folder and open it in VScode
step 2: install Playwright 
  search in VScode extension 
  install Playwright test for VSCode
  search '>playwright' in search bar
  click 'Test: Install Playwright'
  click 'OK' with default ticked options      //it would output blabla with 'Happy hacking!' in terminal which means successful
step 3: install Cucumber plugin in VScode
  $ npm install --save-dev @cucumber/cucumber
  $ npm list @cucumber/cucumber
  $ npx cucumber-js --version
step 4: delete tests folder and playwright.config.ts
step 5: install dependencies
  $ npm i @cucumber/cucumber -D
  $ npm i ts-node -D
step 6: create a project structure
  create a folder under project folder called 'src/test'
  create two folders 'feature' and 'steps' under 'src/test'
  files in 'feature' are plain texts user cases
  files in 'steps' are in TS or JS which are converted from features
  we use cucumber runner file which is in Json... (where?)
